        "text": "The rule that licenses proof by contradiction in its strong form: assume not p, derive a contradiction, conclude p. Classically equivalent to F:excluded-middle and, like it, not intuitionistically valid, so the classical entry in the axiom footprint is again load-bearing. Note what is NOT recorded here: the converse introduction direction (p implies not not p) is constructively fine, and our formalism has no way to mark that asymmetry on a per-direction basis.\n\nOn the axiom footprint: it names the trust base of the SMT ROUTE that established this fact -- the axeyum-ir Boolean evaluator, and the two-valued semantics of the SMT-LIB Bool sort that makes exhaustive truth-table enumeration a proof. It is deliberately NOT empty and deliberately NOT a Lean axiom list. Nothing here went through axeyum's Lean kernel. Measured 2026-08-14 with `cargo run -q -p axeyum-lean-kernel --example nat_axiom_inventory`: the `logic` prelude reports axiom=0 opaque=0 quotient=0, and its declarations are exactly True, False, And, Or, Iff, Not (as `a -> False`), Eq and Exists -- an intuitionistic core with no `Classical.em`, no `propext` and no `Quot.sound`. Zero trusted declarations there means the kernel assumes nothing, not that it can prove everything.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
